  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.03228v1</id>
    <title>AnchorComplete: Recovering Complete Scene Meshes from Partial Point Clouds</title>
    <updated>2026-11-02T14:48:09Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.03228v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.03228v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Most image-based 3D reconstructors primarily recover visible surfaces, producing partial point clouds with large holes and leaving unobserved geometry unresolved. To address this limitation, we introduce AnchorComplete, a framework that reconstructs complete scene meshes from partial point clouds while preserving observed geometry and supporting scenes of varying scales. Building on TRELLIS.2, our method combines partial-point conditioning, which integrates global scene tokens with local spatial evidence to anchor generation to the input, and metric-scale coarse-to-fine generation, which progressively refines scene geometry within fixed-size windows while maintaining global structural consistency. Experiments on Replica and SCRREAM demonstrate that AnchorComplete consistently outperforms strong baselines in complete-scene reconstruction, particularly under sparse-view settings.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CV" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-11-02T14:48:09Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>Project page: https://wrchen530.github.io/anchor-complete</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.CV"/>
    <author>
      <name>Weirong Chen</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Ismail El-Yamany</name>
    </author>
