  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06042v1</id>
    <title>UniRestorer++: Scalable Universal Image Restoration with Multi-Granularity Degradation Modeling</title>
    <updated>2026-11-04T06:46:47Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06042v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.06042v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Universal image restoration aims to handle diverse degradations within a single model, but a reliable scaling strategy remains underexplored. Increasing backbone depth and width can lead to performance saturation, while degradation-aware specialization depends on accurate degradation estimation and is vulnerable to errors on out-of-distribution and real-world inputs. We propose UniRestorer++, a scalable framework based on multi-granularity degradation modeling. It progressively refines degradation groups and introduces group-specific experts, coupling capacity growth with specialization. Degradation-estimation-based routing selects a root-to-leaf path, while granularity-estimation-based routing chooses a level along that path to balance specialization and robustness. Spatially dense degradation representation maps further enable region-aware routing for spatially non-uniform corruptions. We develop CDD-50, a benchmark covering 50 degradation categories from single to penta-degradation. Experiments show approximately log-linear PSNR trends over the evaluated model-size range and stronger scaling gains on out-of-distribution and real-world data than vanilla MoE scaling. UniRestorer++ achieves state-of-the-art performance across benchmarks and demonstrates zero-shot generalization and few-shot transfer on real-world images. Code: https://github.com/mrluin/UniRestorer_plusplus</summary>
    <category term="cs.CV" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-11-04T06:46:47Z</published>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.CV"/>
    <author>
      <name>Jingbo Lin</name>
    </author>
    <author>
