  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06976v1</id>
    <title>On the Opportunities and Challenges of Prefill-to-Autoregressive Cross-Model Transfer</title>
    <updated>2026-11-04T13:33:47Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06976v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.06976v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Prefill-to-Autoregressive Cross-model Transfer (PACT), a form of latent communication between language models, combines a larger model's prompt representations with a smaller model's efficient generation, offering a promising way to balance capability and inference cost. However, existing systems provide limited support for independently evaluating large-small model collaboration, and improved task performance alone does not establish whether the receiver benefits from the sender's information. We introduce PLatour, an open-source PACT framework that connects frozen models through lightweight, zero-initialized linear bridges trained directly with task rewards and supports hybrid-attention architectures. PLatour significantly outperforms open-source baselines on generation tasks and surpasses Mostik's reported results on shared mathematics and coding benchmarks using a substantially smaller sender. However, controlled experiments show that the gains on some tasks can be reproduced by uninformative sender signals, self-communication, or receiver-only training. We find that trainable bridges can act as parameter-efficient adaptation mechanisms without exploiting useful sender information. We therefore propose PACT-Check to quantify how much of a trained PACT system's gain genuinely comes from communication. Finally, we discuss the opportunities and challenges of PACT systems. Code is available at https://github.com/zhenyi4/platour.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-11-04T13:33:47Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>35 pages</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.CL"/>
